    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0677" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg561"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12464.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister to
                            Mexico<anchor n="49" xml:id="d816-f1"/> to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. I beg to inform the Department that day before yesterday the protocol signed
                    at Niagara Falls<anchor n="50" xml:id="d816-f2"/> was read before Congress and
                    that to-day Licenciado Francisco Carbajal, Chief Justice of the Suprenn Court,
                    was appointed Minister for Foreign Affairs and according to reliable information
                    he will become Provisional President.</p>
                <p>For my guidance, and if agreeable to the Department, I should like to learn its
                    views in the event of the above-mentioned change.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d816-f1" n="49" type="source" xml:id="d816-f1-content">
                <p>Representing the interests of the United States in Mexico; see “Severance of
                    diplomatic relations between the United States and Mexico, etc.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d816-f2" n="50" xml:id="d816-f2-content">
                <p>Protocol No. 4; see <ref target="#pg553">page 553</ref>. For the text of Protocol
                    No. 4, concluding the proposal of the Mediators, see <ref target="#pg548">page
                        548</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
